# Rankify-PDF2CBT — env example
# Copy to .env.local (Vercel: Project Settings → Environment Variables)
# All 3 are SERVER-ONLY — never prefix with VITE_ / NUXT_PUBLIC_. Via Vercel Functions /api/*/chat hides them.

# --- Primary fallback (server-side, recommended) ---
# When set on Vercel, clients can call /api/mistral/chat with viaProxy=true without sending Authorization header.
# If unset, client MUST send Authorization: Bearer <key> (BYOK) — see src/lib/providers/README.md
MISTRAL_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
NVIDIA_API_KEY=

# --- Optional: Generic ---
# NODE_ENV=production

# --- Optional: Analytics / telemetry (client, only if you add posthog-js) ---
# VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=
# VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# --- Notes ---
# Preconfigured providers live in src/config/providers.yaml (edit on GitHub).
# Each preset declares its own "envKey" — the Vercel env var name above.
# When a user leaves the client key blank, requests route through
# /api/agent/chat which reads that env var server-side. Users can also add
# private local providers in-browser (Extract → AI Agent → Settings).
# Docs:
#  Mistral  https://docs.mistral.ai/api/endpoint/chat
#  Groq     https://console.groq.com/docs/api-reference
#  NVIDIA   https://docs.api.nvidia.com/nim/reference/create_chat_completion_v1_chat_completions_post-1
